  <p class="standfirst">Paid media buys reach. It doesn't leave anything behind when the campaigns stop.</p>

  <section class="tldr" aria-label="Summary">
    <h2>TL;DR</h2>
    <p>Growing brands spend hundreds of thousands a year acquiring customers through paid media while chronically underinvesting in the information those customers need to evaluate them. A paid ad can introduce someone to your brand. It can't answer every question they have.</p>
    <p>Paid media gets you reach. Authoritative content gives customers, and the AI systems helping them decide, something to evaluate. The goal isn't replacing performance marketing. It's building an owned information asset while you're paying for growth.</p>
    <p><strong>Don't stop renting attention. Start building something alongside it.</strong></p>
  </section>

